<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Farmer sales gather pace.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Farmer sales gather pace.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farmers sales of spring wheat gathered pace on Thursday as the continued slide in prices finally began to prompt some panic, grain dealers in the northern U.S. grain belt said.</p>
<p>&quot;We saw a little bit of panic selling going on today,&quot; one Montana based merchandiser said.</p>
<p>Basis levels were steady to weaker and flat prices sunk sharply as MGE December spring wheat ended off 12-1/2 cents at $3.85-3/4 a bushel.</p>
<p>&quot;A lot of high protein wheat is showing up and there is not much demand,&quot; a Minnesota based merchandiser said.  </p>
